# LIMO pipeline-register data model (M2)

Matches `src/core/pipeline.js`. Every register has `valid`; `valid:false` is a **bubble**
(all control signals 0, so it can change nothing). `pc`, `seq` (fetch order) and `text`
travel with each instruction for the datapath view and the pipeline chart only; hardware
would not need them.

| Register | Fields | Why each field exists |
|---|---|---|
| **IF/ID** | `pc`, `pcPlus4`, `instr` | `pc` and `instr` feed decode; `pcPlus4` is shown on the datapath |
| **ID/EX** | `rs1`, `rs2`, `rd`, `rv1`, `rv2`, `imm`, `pc`, `ctrl{regWrite, aluSrc, aluOp, memRead, memWrite, memToReg, branch, usesRs1, usesRs2}` | `rv1/rv2` = register values read in ID; `rs1/rs2` are kept ONLY so the forwarding unit can compare them with the later `rd` values; `pc`+`imm` give the branch target in EX |
| **EX/MEM** | `aluResult`, `rv2`, `rd`, `branchTaken`, `branchTarget`, `ctrl{regWrite, memRead, memWrite, memToReg}` | `aluResult` is the address (lw/sw) or result; `rv2` (after forwarding) is the store data; `branchTaken` = PCSrc, kept for display because the PC is already redirected in the same cycle |
| **MEM/WB** | `memData`, `aluResult`, `rd`, `ctrl{regWrite, memToReg}` | the MemtoReg mux picks `memData` or `aluResult` for write-back |

**Control signals consumed early are dropped:** `aluSrc`, `aluOp`, `branch` are used in EX and not
copied to EX/MEM; `memRead`/`memWrite` are used in MEM and not copied to MEM/WB; only `regWrite`
and `memToReg` reach WB. `usesRs1/usesRs2` live only in ID/EX (forwarding and stall decisions).

**Where forwarding gets its register numbers:** `rs1/rs2` from ID/EX (consumer) against `rd` in
EX/MEM and MEM/WB (producers). x0 is never forwarded.

**Architectural state (the ISA specifies):** 16 registers, PC, instruction and data memory.
**Microarchitectural state (the ISA must not specify):** the four pipeline registers above, the
stall/flush logic. Different implementations (a 3-stage or 7-stage LIMO) must run the same programs
with the same results, only at different cycle counts. This is your A6(b) answer.

